lucas-acc/signal-track  0.0.2 -> 0.0.3
change_type: instructions+code   changelog: - Added required_config_paths section specifying both preferred (`~/.openclaw/openclaw.json`) and legacy (`~/.signal-track/config.json`) config file locations, with usage notes for each. - Clarified that API base URL is now `https://younews.k.sohu.com/` (was `http://` previously). - Updated execution notes detailing config file reading/writing logic and enhanced description of legacy config fallback. - No functional CLI or feature changes; documentation update only.

### SKILL.md  [instructions]
- ### Global behavior
- - Add `--json` for machine-readable output.
- - `--scope` must be `my` or `square`.
- - For commands requiring authentication, login context is read from:
-   - `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json`
-   - then `~/.younews/config.json`.
- - Authorization header is sent as `Authorization: Bearer <api_key>`.
-   - API base URL defaults to `http://younews.k.sohu.com/`.
- - If `--json` is missing, output is human-readable JSON-style pretty print except for special card-get behavior where the first card is printed.
+   required_config_paths:
+     - path: ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json
+       note: Primary config file. If present, signal-track reads/writes `skills.entries.signal-track.apiKey`.
+     - path: ~/.signal-track/config.json
+       note: Legacy config fallback path used for backwards compatibility.
+ - API base URL defaults to `https://younews.k.sohu.com/`.
+ - Required local config state:
+   - Reads auth from `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` (preferred). If absent, falls back to legacy `~/.signal-track/config.json`.
+   - Writes login state to the detected existing config path (`openclaw` if present, otherwise legacy config path).
+  - If `--json` is missing, output is human-readable JSON-style pretty print except for special card-get behavior where the first card is printed.

